<deviceset name="ADC_ADS1015" prefix="U" uservalue="yes">
<description>&lt;b&gt;ADS1015 - 12-bit 4-Channel I2C ADC with Internal PGA&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;VDD: 2.0-5.5V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sampling Rate: 3.3ksps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain Settings: 2/3, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I2C Address: ADDR low = 1001000x, ADDR high = 1001001x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Internal Comparator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ADS1015 includes an internal comparator that can be set to output a high-level on ALERT when the conversion results exceeeds a pre-defined upper level, and will deassert itself when the level falls below a pre-defined lower threshold level. It can also be set to windowed mode where the ALERT pin will be asserted if the data exceeds the upper threshold or falls below the lower threshold.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
<gates>
<gate name="G$1" symbol="ADS1015" x="0" y="0"/>
</gates>
<devices>
<device name="" package="MSOP10">
<connects>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="ADDR" pad="1"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN0" pad="4"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN1" pad="5"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN2" pad="6"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN3" pad="7"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="ALERT" pad="2"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="GND" pad="3"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="SCL" pad="10"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="SDA" pad="9"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="VDD" pad="8"/>
</connects>
<technologies>
<technology name=""/>
</technologies>
</device>
</devices>
</deviceset>
<deviceset name="ADC_ADS7924" prefix="U" uservalue="yes">
<description>&lt;b&gt;ADS7924 - 12-bit 4-Channel I2C ADC&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AVDD: 2.2-5.5V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DVDD: 1.65V-5.5V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sampling Rate: 100ksps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I2C Address: ADDR low = 1001000x, ADDR DVDD = 1001001x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Digital Threshold Comparators&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ADS794 is a relatively low-power device and can be useful in certain low-power scenarios since it can be configured to regularly check the voltage on the analog input pins, and throw an interrupt or pull an MCU out of reset when a specific condition is met.  Each of the four inputs has it's own programmable threshold level.  It could be used to monitor the input level of solar or other ambient energy sources, and when the level is sufficiently high, wakeup the MCU to perform read some sensor data, etc., or wait until a supercap is charged to a sufficiently high level before waking the MCU.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
<gates>
<gate name="G$1" symbol="ADS7924" x="0" y="0"/>
</gates>
<devices>
<device name="" package="WQFN16">
<connects>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="A0" pad="P$5"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="ADCIN" pad="P$14"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AGND" pad="P$8"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN0" pad="P$12"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN1" pad="P$11"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN2" pad="P$10"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AIN3" pad="P$9"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="AVDD" pad="P$15"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="DGND" pad="P$6"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="DVDD" pad="P$16"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="INT" pad="P$2"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="MUXOUT" pad="P$13"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="PWRCON" pad="P$7"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="RESET" pad="P$1"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="SCL" pad="P$3"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="SDA" pad="P$4"/>
<connect gate="G$1" pin="THERMAL" pad="P$17"/>
</connects>
